&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a French consulting and engineering firm specializing in data and AI, and a leader in Europe. Headquartered in Paris, we are now present in 23 countries across all continents, with a team of 1,700 employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to help businesses unlock the full potential of AI and data by developing tailor-made solutions that address their specific industry challenges. As pioneers in this field, we combine technological expertise with operational excellence, working alongside the world&#39;s leading market players. Our clients span all key economic sectors - industry, retail, luxury, consumer goods, healthcare, and finance - and include major international corporations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Data Analytics Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join our Data Analytics Chapter, a team of 60 professionals with expertise across dashboarding, analytics engineering, marketing measurement, and low-code data science. We are one of three technical teams at Artefact (alongside Software Engineering and Data Science), forming a tech community of 160 people. Despite working on different client engagements, we maintain a strong culture of knowledge sharing through dedicated communities of practice. We are growing fast, with the ambition to double our team size over the next five years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing - Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Data Analyst, you will transform our clients&#39; businesses through effective data collection, processing, and visualization, acting as a trusted advisor for business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivering end-to-end analytics projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frame use cases with business teams, validate data availability, and define the right approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement dashboards, data products, and pipelines that drive business decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving technical excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into scalable analytics architectures and pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply modern analytics engineering practices and promote best practices in data modeling and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leveraging the latest GenAI developments in order to deliver the maximum value possible for our clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being a trusted advisor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract valuable insights and communicate them in clear, actionable terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with client stakeholders and act as a go-to expert for analytics guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contributing to team development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior data analysts and share best practices through workshops and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal accelerators and maintain active technology watch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications - What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for profiles with deep expertise in one of the following domains, combined with openness to work across others. Our flexible career track allows you to specialize or develop a broader skill set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on experience in a data-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in at least one of the following domains:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dashboarding &amp;amp; Data Visualization: &lt;/strong&gt;Power BI, Looker, Tableau, or Superset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics Engineering: &lt;/strong&gt;dbt, with experience on BigQuery, Snowflake, or Databricks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Analytics &amp;amp; Measurement: &lt;/strong&gt;CDP platforms (Treasure Data, Hightouch, Tealium), MMM, attribution, clean rooms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Low-Code / No-Code Data Science: &lt;/strong&gt;Dataiku, Copilot Studio, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundation in SQL and Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Git and software engineering fundamentals (versioning, testing, code quality).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in cloud environments (GCP, Azure, or AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with generative AI applied to analytics (MCP for BI, conversational data interfaces), exposure to multiple domains above, knowledge of statistics and machine learning fundamentals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond technical expertise, we value: intellectual curiosity, pragmatism and creativity, ability to bridge business and technical teams, autonomy and reliability, and clear communication to build client trust.&lt;/p&gt;
